WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.001
Concurrent data structures need several forms of evidence.

2
00:00:03.001 --> 00:00:10.502
ThreadSanitizer can reveal many data races, and it should be part of the engineering toolkit when the platform allows it.

3
00:00:10.502 --> 00:00:15.378
But a clean sanitizer run does not prove that the design is correct.

4
00:00:15.378 --> 00:00:24.755
A program can be free of low-level data races and still violate a higher-level invariant, return stale access, mishandle shutdown, leak resources, or

5
00:00:24.755 --> 00:00:25.881
starve important work.

6
00:00:25.881 --> 00:00:29.631
Diagnostics help, but they do not replace a clear contract.

7
00:00:29.631 --> 00:00:34.132
Testing should cover lifecycle and boundary behavior, not only the common path.

8
00:00:34.132 --> 00:00:40.509
Empty structures, full structures, repeated start and stop cycles, cancellation, producer shutdown, consumer shutdown, eviction, replacement, and

9
00:00:40.509 --> 00:00:42.759
destruction under load all deserve attention.

10
00:00:42.759 --> 00:00:50.261
Stress tests can increase the chance of exposing timing-sensitive defects, especially when combined with randomized operation mixes and invariant

11
00:00:50.261 --> 00:00:50.636
checks.

12
00:00:50.636 --> 00:00:58.513
Logging and metrics can also help identify queue growth, lock contention, unusually long waits, or unexpected cleanup delays in real deployments.

13
00:00:58.513 --> 00:01:01.513
Performance review is valuable when it is disciplined.

14
00:01:01.513 --> 00:01:09.765
Benchmark the behavior that matters, including contention levels and realistic workloads, but do not use speed as a reason to weaken semantics

15
00:01:09.765 --> 00:01:11.266
without documenting the risk.

16
00:01:11.266 --> 00:01:19.892
Code review should ask direct questions: which lock protects which data, what can a caller retain, what happens during shutdown, how are objects

17
00:01:19.892 --> 00:01:24.018
reclaimed, and which tests would fail if the invariant were broken?

18
00:01:24.018 --> 00:01:31.145
Concurrent data structure safety is maintained through design, diagnostics, testing, review, and continuing governance as the structure gains new

19
00:01:31.145 --> 00:01:31.520
users.
